# smart-city-platform

Project Idea: India Urban Intelligence Lakehouse Platform

A real-world, enterprise-grade multi-cloud data engineering platform that ingests, governs, validates, catalogs, streams, transforms, secures, and serves urban intelligence data for Indian cities.

This is not a generic “sales dashboard” project.
It simulates what a 5+ years experienced Data Engineer / Senior Data Engineer / Platform Engineer would actually build in a real company.

Real-World Problem Statement

Indian cities generate massive real-time and batch data from:

Weather APIs
AQI/Pollution APIs
Traffic APIs
EV charging stations
Metro/train/bus live feeds
Smart electricity usage
Open government datasets
News/social sentiment
Public transport GPS feeds
Water level/flood monitoring
Event/tourism spikes
Energy demand
Road accidents

But today:

Data is fragmented
No centralized governance
No trusted quality framework
No lineage
No streaming analytics
No unified catalog
No observability
No multi-cloud resilience
Your Solution

Build a:

Unified Smart City Data Platform

that:

ingests streaming + batch data
performs quality checks
catalogs datasets automatically
applies governance rules
provisions infra using Terraform
deploys using CI/CD
handles observability
supports ML/analytics
enables real-time dashboards
supports multi-cloud disaster recovery

This becomes a resume-defining flagship project.

